  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Landscapes Forum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Healthy ecosystems maintain human livelihoods, counteract global climate change and protect biodiversity. To stop the increasing global degradation of ecosystems, strong networks and partnerships are needed. The Global Landscapes Forum (GLF) is the world&apos;s largest knowledge-led multi-stakeholder platform for integrated, sustainable land use. The project helped to establish the GLF community as a global and regional accelerator of good practices in sustainable landscape approaches. Furthermore, it was instrumental in supporting the preparation and implementation of the UN Decade on Ecosystem Restoration 2021-2030. For this purpose, the project engaged a broad group of stakeholders at all levels. It also developed inclusive guidelines and programs to provide local communities with practical tools and knowledge to initiate and scale up restoration actions.</narrative>
  </description>
